      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `intent_id`: str (required) - `tool_name`: RuntimeToolName (required) - `payload`: dict[str, Any] (default {}) - `requested_paths`: list[str] (default []) - `require_worktree`: bool (default False) - `allow_main_repo_mutation`: bool (default False)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-20",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "RuntimeToolInvocationEnvelope",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `schema_version`: str (const `rig.relay.runtime_tool_invocation.v1`) - `invocation_id`: str (required) - `intent_id`: str (required) - `tool_name`: RuntimeToolName (required) - `status`: RuntimeToolInvocationStatus (required) - `session_id`, `task_id`, `lane_id`, `workspace_id`: optional str - `worktree_path`, `repo_root`, `cwd`: optional str - `payload`: dict[str, Any] - `requested_paths`: list[str] - `error_kind`, `refusal_reason`: optional",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "All models use `extra=\"forbid\"` and stable StrEnum serialization.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-23",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Adapter: `prepare()` Method",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Signature:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "code-25",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "def prepare(\n    self,\n    intent: RuntimeToolIntent,\n    resolution: RuntimeContextResolution,\n) -> RuntimeToolInvocationEnvelope",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "detailed",
        "collapsible": true,
        "collapsed_by_default": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Behavior: 1. If resolution is blocked/refused → BLOCKED with CONTEXT_UNRESOLVED 2. If context is None → BLOCKED with CONTEXT_UNRESOLVED 3. If require_worktree and no worktree_path → BLOCKED with WORKTREE_REQUIRED 4. Resolve cwd: worktree_path → repo_root → None 5. If mutation tool and no worktree without allow_main_repo_mutation → REFUSED with UNSUPPORTED_MUTATION_LOCATION 6. Validate paths against repo/worktree scope → REFUSED with UNSAFE_PATH 7. Delegate to tool-specific handler",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-27",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Tool-Specific Behavior",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-28",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "write_file",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Requires `path` and `content` in payload - If `allow_overwrite_protected=True` without `expected_before_sha256` → REFUSED with EXPECTED_HASH_MISSING - Uses worktree cwd when available",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-30",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "search_replace",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-31",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Requires `file_path` (or `file`) in payload - Preserves canonical session/task metadata - Refuses mutation into main repo without `allow_main_repo_mutation=True`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-32",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "validate",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-33",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Defaults profile to `\"quick\"` if not specified - Injects `workspace_root` from cwd if not set - Injects `paths` from intent's requested_paths if not set - Injects `expected_dirty_policy` from context if not set",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-34",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "runtime_exec",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Requires `argv` as non-empty list of strings - Validates payload shape by constructing an `ExecutionRequest` model (no persistence) - Puts ExecutionRequest fields flat in the payload (not nested under `_execution_request`) - Does NOT acquire lease or execute",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-36",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "bash_legacy",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Refused by default unless `legacy_fallback_allowed=True` in payload - When allowed, requires `command` in payload",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-38",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Raw Payload vs Receipt Boundary",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-39",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Invocation envelopes carry operational input payloads that the tool needs to execute (file content, SEARCH/REPLACE blocks, argv). These are NOT content-light. Receipts, audit events, and projection integrity assessments derived from these envelopes MUST be content-light — they must not carry raw payloads.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-40",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Schema",
      "disclosure": {
